reagent-name-zoleadone = zoleadone
reagent-desc-zoleadone = A cryogenics chemical, commonly used to treat complex fractures. Works even if the patient is dead.

reagent-name-cyclogenol = cyclogenol
reagent-desc-cyclogenol = A curious crystalline solution brewed at low temperatures. It isn't useful on its own, though the delicate crystals can be interesting to observe.

reagent-name-recyclogenix = recyclogenix
reagent-desc-recyclogenix = An experimental gene therapy drug capable of reverting large-scale cellular mutations. Mechanisms inside the body are only stable at low temperatures.

reagent-name-cytogenecin = cytogenecin
reagent-desc-cytogenecin = A byproduct of recyclogenix's metabolism, this chemical flushes waste from the mutagenic reversion process from the blood and body.
